# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# udisks2 is on the box so the host helper can list USB drives and mount one when the owner asks. It never mounts a
# plugged-in drive by itself (the daemon does not; desktop helpers such as gvfs or udiskie do, and none is installed).
# This hint tells any such client the same: UDISKS_AUTO=0 means "do not automount". Runs before 80-udisks2.rules.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", ENV{UDISKS_AUTO}="0"
